Goal: close the pinned Java 5.5.1 producer and Broker diagnostics RPC/DTO
slice within Phase 18, on branch `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`.

Changes:
- Added `MQClientApi::get_producer_connection_list`,
  `get_all_producer_info`, and `get_broker_runtime_info` for request codes 204,
  328, and 28. They set Java language, apply configured VIP port translation,
  preserve the supplied address in typed response errors, and decode nullable
  success bodies.
- Added Java-compatible `ProducerConnection`, `ProducerInfo`,
  `ProducerTableInfo`, and `KvTable` response models, including Java defaults,
  explicit null behavior, mutable collection aliases, public method inventories,
  and `ProducerInfo.toString()` behavior.
- Added invoked Java 5.5.1 fixtures, Rust RPC comparisons, request-code
  crosswalk entries, compatibility evidence, and release checklist results.

Verification passed:
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-core --all-features --locked` (185 unit
  tests, all integration targets, and 16 doctests).
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol -p rocketmq-classic-core
  --all-features --locked producer_diagnostic` (DTO, VIP loopback, and invoked
  Java RPC fixture tests).
- Strict all-target/all-feature Clippy for Common, Protocol, Remoting, Core,
  Producer, Consumer, and the facade with `-D warnings`.
- `mvn -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` (37 invoked RPC scenarios,
  67 typed-header frames, 15 typed-body fixtures, and Java/Rust cross-decodes).
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`
- `git diff --check`

Producer core fixture: `fixtures/producer/core.json`, SHA-256
`85de9ff0aeeb0236d72fa0ecff85ec01cc24ff1b75a64308eddbc0ac5cfe077d`.

This closes only the named producer/Broker diagnostics RPC and DTO slice.
Broad P18-V01 and P18-V02/P18-V03/P18-V04 remain open. Phase 19 working-tree
files were left unstaged and unchanged.
